.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga/payload-ga-4.redacted.txt:2361: | v2.55 | ADR-110-AMEND-2 §1.6 (pair-rail timeout recalibration 120/150 → 180/210 s, S291 ceremony 2026-08-03) — NO new action (`_KNOWN_ACTIONS` stays 324) and no new allowlist. ONE new bounded field `timeout_ms` (int 0..6000000 — the EFFECTIVE POST-CLAMP codex budget the invocation ran under) added to the EXISTING `pair_rail_case` AND `pair_rail_review_expected` allowlists, coerced in both typed wrappers AND both `emit_generic` dispatch branches (never `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`). Motivation is the §4(i) named residual: no event recorded the effective budget, so a session exporting `CEO_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_S=5` produced a case F byte-INDISTINGUISHABLE from a genuine Codex outage — making the undocumented knob stealthier than the documented `CEO_PAIR_RAIL_DISABLE` kill-switch, which emits its own loud event. A minimum floor on the knob stays DEFERRED (changing a documented knob's semantics is a new contract, AMEND-1 consensus item 2), but the incentive gradient is no longer inverted and the next amendment's historical series is no longer born ambiguous. **Encoding is normative, not stylistic:** MILLISECONDS as an int, NOT the float seconds the amendment prose names — `_lib/canonical_json.py` rejects floats in HMAC-covered fields, and the spool writer then drops the ENTIRE event leaving only an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb, which on these two actions would manufacture the exact /ceo-boot S254 liveness deficit they exist to measure. Same encoding + rationale as `dispatcher_route.wall_clock_ms` (PLAN-081 Phase 2, Codex iter 1 P0-1). The HMAC chain shape + `verify_chain()` are UNTOUCHED. | *(1 new bounded int field on 2 existing actions; no new actions, no new allowlists; shared coercion `_coerce_pair_rail_timeout_ms` + bound `_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_MS_MAX` in `audit_emit.py`)* |
